@event elixir_trunk
# en: The Bottle in Your Trunk
title [03c728] = 箱子里的瓶子
# en: {has(brightwater_bottle) and has(owls_ink_bottle): Under your spare robes, wrapped in two socks, the bottles wait, one gold and one black.|{Under your spare robes, wrapped in a sock, the bottle waits.|The bottle is still in your trunk. You have checked on it more often than on your homework.|You know exactly where the bottle is without looking.}} {has(brightwater_want) or has(owls_ink_want): Since the last dose wore off, it has been very easy to think about.|{before_finals(): Finals are close.|Nobody knows it's there, you're nearly sure.}}
text [20a0b4] = {has(brightwater_bottle) and has(owls_ink_bottle): 在你备用的长袍底下，裹在两只袜子里，两只瓶子在等着，一金一黑。|{在你备用的长袍底下，裹在一只袜子里，那只瓶子在等着。|瓶子还在你的箱子里。你检查它的次数，比检查作业还多。|你不用看也知道瓶子在哪儿。}} {has(brightwater_want) or has(owls_ink_want): 上一剂的劲儿过去以后，想起它变得太容易了。|{before_finals(): 期末快到了。|没人知道它在那儿，你几乎可以肯定。}}
# en: A student kneeling at an open school trunk at night, a small stoppered bottle in a sock in one hand, a candle on the floor beside them.
scene [4f544f] = 夜里，一个学生跪在打开的学生箱前，一手拿着裹在袜子里的小塞瓶，地上放着一支蜡烛。
# en: Drink the Brightwater
opt.bright.label [26149d] = 喝下亮泉水
# en: Two good months. After that, maybe not.
opt.bright.hint [2a9571] = 两个好月份。之后，就不一定了。
# en: {It tastes of honey and pennies. Within the hour you're warm to your fingertips, and the day ahead looks easy.|You drink it at the window. The tiredness lifts like a lid. You know it's borrowed, and you don't mind yet.|One swallow, and everything that ached stops. You hide the empty bottle at the bottom of the trunk.}
opt.bright.say.1 [e405ab] = {它尝起来像蜂蜜和铜板。不到一个钟头，你从头暖到指尖，接下来的日子看起来很轻松。|你站在窗边喝下它。疲惫像盖子一样被揭开了。你知道这是借来的，但暂时还不在乎。|一口下去，所有酸痛都停了。你把空瓶藏到箱子最底下。}
# en: Drink the Owl's Ink
opt.ink.label [e516da] = 喝下枭墨
# en: Two sharp months, exams included. After that, maybe not.
opt.ink.hint [b0c0ec] = 两个清醒的月份，考试也算在内。之后，就不一定了。
# en: {It's bitter as a burnt quill. By morning your head is a lamp-lit room, every shelf in order, and magic hums in your fingers.|You drink it standing up. The words on your desk sharpen, line by line, like a page coming into focus.|Black, bitter, and then clear. You read three chapters before breakfast and remember every word of them.}
opt.ink.say.1 [306ce7] = {苦得像烧焦的羽毛笔。到早上，你的脑子成了一间点着灯的屋子，每一层书架都井井有条，魔力在指尖嗡嗡作响。|你站着把它喝了。桌上的字一行一行变得清晰，像一页纸慢慢对上了焦。|黑的，苦的，然后一切清楚了。早饭前你读完了三章，每个字都记得。}
# en: Pour the Brightwater away
opt.pour_bright.label [7f06a3] = 把亮泉水倒掉
# en: {You tip the gold out of the window into the ivy. The ivy, next morning, is a remarkable colour.|You pour the gold down the washbasin and run the tap for a long time afterwards. You feel lighter, and worse.|Out of the window, every gold drop. You watch it go and want it back the whole time.}
opt.pour_bright.say.1 [19c6d7] = {你把那金色的东西从窗口倒进常春藤里。第二天早上，那片常春藤的颜色非同寻常。|你把那金色的东西倒进洗脸盆，然后开着水龙头冲了很久。你觉得轻松了，也觉得更糟了。|每一滴金色都倒出了窗外。你看着它流走，从头到尾都想把它要回来。}
# en: Pour the Owl's Ink away
opt.pour_ink.label [77383a] = 把枭墨倒掉
# en: {You tip the black out of the window into the ivy. By morning the leaves it touched have curled up tight.|You pour the black down the washbasin, and it stains the porcelain grey. You scrub until it's gone.|Out of the window, every black drop. Finals will be exactly as hard as they are.}
opt.pour_ink.say.1 [4cb8f6] = {你把那黑色的东西从窗口倒进常春藤里。到早上，沾到它的叶子都紧紧卷了起来。|你把那黑色的东西倒进洗脸盆，瓷面被染成了灰色。你一直擦到看不出来为止。|每一滴黑色都倒出了窗外。期末会和它本来一样难。}
# en: Not yet
opt.wait.label [8dd27c] = 还不到时候
# en: {You wrap it up again and close the lid.|Not tonight. You put the trunk back under the bed and lie awake knowing where it is.|You leave it where it is, for now. For a better reason, later.}
opt.wait.say.1 [7a1dfc] = {你把它重新裹好，合上箱盖。|今晚不喝。你把箱子推回床底，躺着睡不着，心里清楚它在哪儿。|你暂时不动它。以后，会有更好的理由。}

@event elixir_offered_bright
# en: Something for the Grey Days
title [6c63d1] = 留给阴天的东西
# en: {other} has been glowing for a week: sleeping well, laughing loudly, top of every drill. In the corridor {they} put{s} a small cloudy-gold bottle in your hand. "Brightwater. From the village. It's only banned because it works."
text [7d2d71] = {other}已经容光焕发一个星期了：睡得好，笑得响，每次操练都拿第一。在走廊里，{they}把一只浑浊金色的小瓶塞进你手里。“亮泉水。村里来的。它被禁，只是因为太管用了。”
# en: A school corridor, one student pressing a small cloudy-gold bottle into another student's hand, glancing down the corridor for prefects.
scene [288b21] = 学校走廊里，一个学生把一只浑浊金色的小瓶塞进另一个学生手里，一边往走廊那头张望有没有级长。
# en: Keep it, for a grey day
opt.left.label [3db690] = 收下，留给阴天
# en: You wrap it in a sock and bury it in your trunk. It feels heavier there than it did in your hand.
opt.left.say.1 [8bfbc7] = 你把它裹进袜子，埋在箱子里。它在那儿比在你手里时更沉。
# en: Give it back
opt.right.label [b4bc84] = 还回去
# en: "Suit yourself," says {other}, and pockets it, a little stung. For a day or two {they} look{s} at you as if you'd said something unkind.
opt.right.say.1 [86a32e] = “随你，”{other}说着把它揣回兜里，有点受伤。之后一两天，{they}看你的眼神，就像你说了什么刻薄话。

@event elixir_borrowed_bag
# en: Not Your Bottle
title [f50c67] = 不是你的瓶子
# en: You borrow {other}'s satchel to carry your books to a lecture, and at the bottom of it, wrapped in a sock, is a small black bottle with a village label. Owl's Ink. Everyone knows what it is, and that it's banned.
text [ecf0bc] = 你借了{other}的书包去上课，在包底，裹在一只袜子里，有一只贴着村里标签的小黑瓶。枭墨。人人都知道那是什么，也知道它是违禁的。
# en: A student kneeling over a borrowed satchel, holding up a small black bottle wrapped in a sock, with an uneasy face.
scene [c18af8] = 一个学生跪在借来的书包旁，举起一只裹在袜子里的小黑瓶，脸色不安。
# en: Keep it
opt.left.label [87c2f5] = 留下它
# en: You slip it into your own pocket and give the satchel back with a smile. {other} doesn't say a word. Neither, it turns out, do you, for a week.
opt.left.say.1 [307035] = 你把它塞进自己的口袋，笑着把书包还了回去。{other}一个字也没说。结果，你也一个星期没说。
# en: Give it back, and say why
opt.right.label [4c869c] = 还回去，并说明原因
# en: You hand it back in private. {other} goes red, then quiet, then thanks you, which is the hardest part to listen to.
opt.right.say.1 [47baa7] = 你私下把它还了回去。{other}先是脸红，然后沉默，然后向你道谢，那句谢谢最难听进去。

@event elixir_first_year
# en: A Tonic from Home
title [27c4ee] = 家里带来的补药
# en: A first-year on your corridor has been dancing on the stairs at midnight and sleeping through breakfast. On their windowsill is their "tonic from home": cloudy gold, a village label. You know exactly what it is, and so, by the look of the stairs, does everyone else.
text [feb3c1] = 你那条走廊上的一个一年级生，半夜在楼梯上跳舞，早饭总是睡过头。TA的窗台上放着“家里带来的补药”：浑浊的金色，村里的标签。你很清楚那是什么，看楼梯的样子，别人也都清楚。
# en: A first-year's dormitory windowsill with a cloudy-gold bottle on it, the first-year asleep on top of the covers at midday.
scene [7b6fdf] = 一年级生宿舍的窗台上放着一只浑浊金色的瓶子，那个一年级生正午还和衣睡在被子上。
# en: Buy it off them, quietly
opt.left.label [954bd8] = 悄悄从TA手里买下
# en: You pay a fair price and tell them where it really comes from. They look relieved to be rid of it. Now it's in your trunk instead of theirs.
opt.left.say.1 [393fb3] = 你付了公道的价钱，告诉TA这东西真正是从哪儿来的。TA看起来如释重负。现在它在你的箱子里，而不是TA的箱子里。
# en: Walk them to the infirmary
opt.right.label [6b11df] = 陪TA去医务室
# en: Sister Amaranth takes the bottle in one hand and the first-year in the other. "Good. Next time, come sooner," she tells you. You spend the evening on a hard bench, worrying, until you hear they're all right.
opt.right.say.1 [89c8c0] = 阿玛兰斯修女一手接过瓶子，一手接过那个一年级生。“很好。下次早点来，”她对你说。你在硬板凳上坐了一晚上，提心吊胆，直到听说那孩子没事。

@event elixir_finals_spare
# en: Two Bottles Too Many
title [f5eb25] = 多出来的一瓶
# en: {~{other} catches you on the dormitory stairs, pale and sheepish. In a panic about finals {they} bought two bottles of Owl's Ink from someone behind the refectory, and now want{s} rid of the second. "At cost," {they} say{s}. "Please. I can't have both in my trunk."|{other} sits down next to you in the library and slides a black bottle across the desk behind a book. A cousin in the village sent two. "I only need one to pass," {they} whisper{s}. "At cost. Please."|{other} finds you after supper with a black bottle in each coat pocket, bought off a fifth-year at the Newt at a terrible price. "I panicked," {they} say{s}. "Take one off me at cost? Please?"}
text [9391a1] = {~{other}在宿舍楼梯上拦住你，脸色苍白，一脸窘迫。因为担心期末，{they}慌慌张张地从食堂后面的人手里买了两瓶枭墨，现在想把第二瓶出手。“按原价，”{they}说。“求你了。我的箱子里不能放两瓶。”|{other}在图书馆里坐到你旁边，借一本书挡着，把一只黑瓶推过桌面。村里的一个表亲寄来了两瓶。“我只要一瓶就能及格，”{they}小声说。“按原价。求你了。”|晚饭后{other}找到你，外套两边口袋里各装着一只黑瓶，是在镀金蝾螈酒馆从一个五年级生手里高价买的。“我慌了，”{they}说。“按原价匀一瓶给你？求你了？”}
# en: A student in a dormitory doorway holding out a small black bottle in an open palm, a second identical bottle in the other hand, looking embarrassed.
scene [408c48] = 宿舍门口，一个学生摊开手掌递出一只小黑瓶，另一只手里拿着一模一样的第二瓶，神情尴尬。
# en: Take it off {their} hands
opt.left.label [d81a12] = 替{them}接手
# en: {~The coins go one way and the bottle the other, on the stairs, both of you looking at your shoes. {other} looks lighter for it. You don't.|You slip the bottle inside your book and the coins under {other}'s. Neither of you reads another word that evening.|You take the bottle from {other}'s pocket yourself, so nobody sees it change hands. The price was terrible; you pay it anyway.}
opt.left.say.1 [11eea2] = {~在楼梯上，钱币往一边去，瓶子往另一边去，你们俩都低头看着鞋。{other}看起来轻松了。你没有。|你把瓶子夹进自己的书里，把钱塞到{other}的书底下。那天晚上你们俩谁都没再读进一个字。|你亲手从{other}的口袋里取出瓶子，这样就没人看见它换了手。价钱很离谱；你还是付了。}
# en: Tell {them} to pour them both away
opt.right.label [6c69d6] = 叫{them}把两瓶都倒掉
# en: {~"Both?" says {other}, as if you'd asked {them} to pour away a term's work. {other} goes off to think about it, and won't quite meet your eye for a week.|{other} puts the bottle back behind the book without a word, and spends the rest of the evening reading the same page.|"At that price?" says {other}, appalled, and goes off with a bottle in each pocket, and looks at you sideways at breakfast.}
opt.right.say.1 [0e1358] = {~“两瓶都倒？”{other}说，好像你叫{them}倒掉的是一整个学期的功课。{other}走开去想这件事，之后一个星期都不太敢看你的眼睛。|{other}一言不发地把瓶子放回书后面，整个晚上都在读同一页。|“花了那么多钱？”{other}吓了一跳，口袋里揣着两瓶走了，第二天早饭时斜眼看你。}

@event elixir_finals_buyers
# en: Customers Before Finals
title [84c962] = 期末前的买家
# en: {Word has got round that you have a bottle of Owl's Ink. {buyer} corners you on the stairs, purse already open. "Name your price. I'm going to fail otherwise."|{buyer} has heard about your bottle too, and doesn't haggle.|Finals, and {buyer} on the stairs, purse in hand. Somehow they always know.}
text [98dfdd] = {你有一瓶枭墨的消息传开了。{buyer}在楼梯上堵住你，钱袋已经打开。“你开个价。不然我就要挂科了。”|{buyer}也听说了你的瓶子，而且不还价。|期末，{buyer}拿着钱袋在楼梯上。不知怎么的，他们总会知道。}
# en: A student cornered on a stair landing by a desperate classmate holding out a purse.
scene [437756] = 楼梯平台上，一个学生被一个拿着钱袋、走投无路的同学堵住。
# en: Sell it
opt.left.label [4ac442] = 卖掉
# en: {You sell it. {buyer} holds the bottle like a holy relic and runs. You count the coins twice and don't feel richer.|The bottle changes hands on the landing. Your purse is heavy, and so, for a day or two, is something else.|You sell, and {buyer} thanks you as if you'd done something kind. You haven't.}
opt.left.say.1 [d73a1f] = {你卖了。{buyer}像捧圣物一样捧着瓶子跑了。你把钱数了两遍，并没觉得更富。|瓶子在平台上换了手。你的钱袋沉了，有一两天，别的什么也沉甸甸的。|你卖了，{buyer}向你道谢，好像你做了件好事。你没有。}
# en: Keep it for your own exams
opt.right.label [5dc4d5] = 留着自己考试用
# en: {"It's spoken for," you say. {buyer}'s face falls, and stays fallen for a week.|You keep it. {buyer} calls you something on the way down the stairs, not quite quietly enough.|No sale. {buyer} doesn't believe you need it more, and says so.}
opt.right.say.1 [91f8eb] = {“已经有主了，”你说。{buyer}的脸沉了下去，沉了一个星期。|你留下了它。{buyer}下楼时骂了你一句，声音并不算小。|不卖。{buyer}不相信你比自己更需要它，还说了出来。}

@event grisk_elixir_offer
# en: Grisk's Better Bottles
title [190c46] = 格里斯克的好瓶子
# en: {Grisk beckons you to his corner table, where a gold bottle and a black one stand beside his ledger. "I hear you've a taste for the village's better remedies," he purrs. "I can keep you in them. Not only for money. Between friends, favours keep better. The boathouse jetty, any midnight."|Grisk's corner table, and the two bottles again. "The offer keeps," he says, "like the bottles."|The corner table, the bottles, the little bow from his chair. "Still a friend in need of friends?" he asks.}
text [46cf46] = {格里斯克招手让你到他的角落桌边，账本旁立着一只金瓶和一只黑瓶。“听说你对村里的上等药方有点兴趣，”他柔声说。“我能让你一直不缺。不只收钱。朋友之间，人情比钱更经得住放。船屋码头，哪个午夜都行。”|格里斯克的角落桌，那两只瓶子又在。“这提议一直有效，”他说，“跟这些瓶子一样。”|角落桌，瓶子，他坐在椅子上微微一躬。“还是那个需要朋友的朋友吗？”他问。}
# en: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat at a corner table of a candlelit tavern, a gold bottle and a black one standing on the table beside his ledger.
scene [c6d256] = 烛光昏暗的酒馆角落桌边，一个穿天鹅绒马甲的地精坐着，账本旁立着一只金瓶和一只黑瓶。
# en: Shake his hand
opt.left.label [e76d26] = 和他握手
# en: {His hand is dry and very warm. He slides the gold bottle across the table. "A sample," he says. "Between friends, the first is a gift. The rest, at the jetty."|You shake. Grisk writes something in his ledger with a flourish, and hands you the gold bottle "for goodwill". "Midnight, the jetty," he says. "I keep."|You shake on it. He tucks the black bottle away and gives you the gold one. "The black costs a favour," he says. "Come down to the jetty when you want one."}
opt.left.say.1 [8b1b37] = {他的手干燥而温热。他把金瓶推过桌面。“样品，”他说。“朋友之间，第一瓶是送的。往后的，在码头。”|你们握了手。格里斯克花哨地在账本上写了点什么，把金瓶递给你，“聊表善意”。“午夜，码头，”他说。“我一直都在。”|你们握手成交。他把黑瓶收起来，把金瓶给了你。“黑的要一个人情，”他说。“想要的时候就到码头来。”}
# en: Not interested
opt.right.label [ccbe6d] = 不感兴趣
# en: {"The offer keeps," says Grisk, unoffended, and turns back to his ledger.|He bows you away from the table without getting up. "Another night, then. I'm a patient friend."|"Of course," says Grisk. He doesn't believe you, and he lets you see it.}
opt.right.say.1 [a4e85f] = {“提议一直有效，”格里斯克毫不介意，又低头看他的账本。|他坐着没起身，鞠躬送你离开桌边。“那就改天。我是个有耐心的朋友。”|“当然，”格里斯克说。他不信你，也故意让你看出来。}

@event grisk_elixir_favour
# en: A Bottle for a Favour
title [ab3a91] = 一瓶换一个人情
# en: Grisk has a bottle and a favour, and they come as a pair. {&"Watch the jetty for an hour, and see nothing."|"Keep a crate under your bed till Thursday."|"A kind word to a prefect, about a friend of mine."} {before_finals() or has(brightwater_want) or has(owls_ink_want): "And a few crowns on delivery," he adds. "{before_finals(): Ink is dear this close to finals.|You look like someone who needs a friend, and friends are dear.}"|He smiles. "Small things."}
text [ff7ee2] = 格里斯克手里有一只瓶子和一个人情，两样是配套的。{&“替我看一个钟头码头，什么也别看见。”|“帮我把一只木箱在你床底下放到星期四。”|“替我的一个朋友，在某位级长面前美言一句。”} {before_finals() or has(brightwater_want) or has(owls_ink_want): “交货时再加几个克朗，”他补了一句。“{before_finals(): 离期末这么近，墨可贵了。|你看起来像个需要朋友的人，而朋友是很贵的。}”|他微笑着。“小事而已。”}
# en: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat on a midnight jetty holding up a small bottle between two fingers, a ledger open on a crate beside him.
scene [cf12b3] = 午夜的码头上，一个穿天鹅绒马甲的地精用两根手指夹着一只小瓶举起来，旁边一只木箱上摊着账本。
# en: Owl's Ink, for the favour
opt.ink.label [40d55a] = 用这个人情换枭墨
# en: A few crowns more before finals, and when he knows you need it.
opt.ink.hint [ada41d] = 期末前要多付几个克朗，他知道你需要它时也是。
# en: {&You stand on the jetty for an hour and see nothing, very carefully. At dawn there's a black bottle on your windowsill, with a note that says "Friends."|The crate sits under your bed till Thursday, humming faintly. Then it's gone, and a black bottle is where it stood.|You put in Grisk's word with a prefect, and it lands. The black bottle arrives in your shoe, which you don't like thinking about.}
opt.ink.say.1 [762d35] = {&你在码头站了一个钟头，非常小心地什么也没看见。天亮时窗台上有一只黑瓶，还有一张纸条，上面写着“朋友”。|木箱在你床底下放到星期四，一直在轻轻嗡鸣。然后它不见了，原地放着一只黑瓶。|你替格里斯克在一位级长面前说了话，说成了。黑瓶出现在你的鞋里，你不愿多想这件事。}
# en: {&A prefect's lantern comes down the lawn while you're watching the jetty. You're in their notebook before you've thought of a reason. No bottle; Grisk doesn't pay for failures.|A prefect doing rounds finds the crate under your bed and asks what's in it. You don't know, which is the worst answer. The crate goes, and no bottle comes.|The prefect hears you out, then asks who put you up to it. You don't say, and your name goes in the notebook anyway. Grisk sends only his regrets.}
opt.ink.say.2 [7c238c] = {&你正看着码头，一位级长的提灯从草坪那头过来了。你还没想好理由，名字已经进了小本子。没有瓶子；格里斯克不为失败付账。|一位巡夜的级长发现了你床底下的木箱，问里面是什么。你不知道，这是最糟的回答。木箱被拿走了，瓶子也没来。|级长听完你的话，问是谁让你来的。你没说，名字照样进了小本子。格里斯克只送来他的遗憾。}
# en: Brightwater, for the favour
opt.bright.label [b7f3e9] = 用这个人情换亮泉水
# en: A few crowns more before finals, and when he knows you need it.
opt.bright.hint [ada41d] = 期末前要多付几个克朗，他知道你需要它时也是。
# en: {&You stand on the jetty for an hour and see nothing, very carefully. At dawn there's a gold bottle on your windowsill, with a note that says "Friends."|The crate sits under your bed till Thursday, humming faintly. Then it's gone, and a gold bottle is where it stood.|You put in Grisk's word with a prefect, and it lands. The gold bottle arrives in your shoe, which you don't like thinking about.}
opt.bright.say.1 [8fa2fe] = {&你在码头站了一个钟头，非常小心地什么也没看见。天亮时窗台上有一只金瓶，还有一张纸条，上面写着“朋友”。|木箱在你床底下放到星期四，一直在轻轻嗡鸣。然后它不见了，原地放着一只金瓶。|你替格里斯克在一位级长面前说了话，说成了。金瓶出现在你的鞋里，你不愿多想这件事。}
# en: {&A prefect's lantern comes down the lawn while you're watching the jetty. You're in their notebook before you've thought of a reason. No bottle; Grisk doesn't pay for failures.|A prefect doing rounds finds the crate under your bed and asks what's in it. You don't know, which is the worst answer. The crate goes, and no bottle comes.|The prefect hears you out, then asks who put you up to it. You don't say, and your name goes in the notebook anyway. Grisk sends only his regrets.}
opt.bright.say.2 [7c238c] = {&你正看着码头，一位级长的提灯从草坪那头过来了。你还没想好理由，名字已经进了小本子。没有瓶子；格里斯克不为失败付账。|一位巡夜的级长发现了你床底下的木箱，问里面是什么。你不知道，这是最糟的回答。木箱被拿走了，瓶子也没来。|级长听完你的话，问是谁让你来的。你没说，名字照样进了小本子。格里斯克只送来他的遗憾。}
# en: Tell him you're done
opt.done.label [1b5f57] = 告诉他你不干了
# en: {&"Everyone is, eventually," says Grisk pleasantly, and closes his ledger. "Until they aren't." You walk back up the lawn without a bottle, and it's the longest walk you've had.|Grisk shrugs. "My door doesn't lock," he says. You go back to bed shaking, and proud of it.|"Done," you say. Grisk bows, as if you'd paid him a compliment, and turns the lamp down.}
opt.done.say.1 [27b9d1] = {&“人人最后都会这么说，”格里斯克和气地说，合上账本。“直到他们不再这么说。”你没带瓶子走回草坪，那是你走过最长的一段路。|格里斯克耸耸肩。“我的门不上锁，”他说。你回去睡觉时浑身发抖，也为此骄傲。|“不干了，”你说。格里斯克鞠了一躬，好像你恭维了他，然后把灯拧暗。}
# en: Not this month
opt.none.label [9e6244] = 这个月不要
# en: {&Grisk tucks the bottle away. "Next month, then."|You shake your head. Grisk makes a small note in his ledger, as if you'd ordered something.|"Of course," says Grisk. "I keep."}
opt.none.say.1 [082407] = {&格里斯克把瓶子收起来。“那就下个月。”|你摇摇头。格里斯克在账本上记了一笔，好像你订了什么货。|“当然，”格里斯克说。“我一直都在。”}

@event contraband_caught
# en: A Search at Dawn
title [0602c9] = 黎明搜查
# en: The prefects are going down your corridor at dawn, trunk by trunk, sniffing bottles. {has(brightwater_bottle) or has(owls_ink_bottle): There is a bottle in yours.|Your trunk is clean, nearly, but you know what has been through your hands lately, and the prefect sniffing at the lid looks as if they know it too.}
text [61f1b4] = 天刚亮，级长们正沿着你的走廊一只箱子一只箱子地搜，挨个闻瓶子。{has(brightwater_bottle) or has(owls_ink_bottle): 你的箱子里有一只瓶子。|你的箱子差不多是干净的，可你知道最近有什么经过了你的手，而在箱盖边嗅来嗅去的那位级长，看起来也知道。}
# en: A dormitory corridor at dawn, two prefects in red sashes going through an open school trunk, students in nightclothes watching from their doors.
scene [838f02] = 黎明的宿舍走廊，两个系红肩带的级长在翻一只打开的学生箱，穿睡衣的学生们从门口看着。
# en: Bluff it out
opt.left.label [9cc9e7] = 硬撑过去
# en: You're half asleep and mildly offended, and they believe both. The prefects move on to the next trunk. You sit on the end of your bed until your heart slows down.
opt.left.say.1 [ba9b16] = 你半睡半醒，还有点被冒犯，他们两样都信了。级长们去搜下一只箱子。你坐在床尾，等心跳慢下来。
# en: They find it in under a minute. The bottle goes into a bag labelled for the confiscation vault, your name goes into a notebook, and the whole corridor watches you go red.
opt.left.say.2 [a25840] = 他们不到一分钟就找到了。瓶子进了一只标着“没收库”的袋子，你的名字进了一个小本子，整条走廊都看着你脸红。
# en: There's nothing in the trunk to find, but your face gives you away. You get a warning, a line in the prefect's notebook, and a long look from the whole corridor.
opt.left.say.3 [c5ded6] = 箱子里没什么可找的，可你的脸出卖了你。你得到一次警告，级长的小本子上多了一行，还有整条走廊投来的长长的目光。
# en: Own up before they look
opt.right.label [673e92] = 在他们搜之前主动交出
# en: You hand it over before they reach your trunk. The prefect bags it for the confiscation vault, looks at you for a long moment, and writes only a warning. It still stings.
opt.right.say.1 [e2da48] = 他们还没搜到你的箱子，你就交了出来。级长把它装袋送往没收库，久久地看了你一眼，只记了一次警告。还是很刺痛。
# en: You tell them before they ask. With nothing to confiscate, the prefect writes only a warning, and gives you a long look. It still stings.
opt.right.say.2 [0f4b94] = 他们还没开口，你就说了。没什么可没收的，级长只记了一次警告，久久地看了你一眼。还是很刺痛。

@event contraband_friend_notices
# en: You Don't Look Right
title [664bfb] = 你看起来不对劲
# en: {has(brightwater_want) or has(owls_ink_want): {~{friend} catches your wrist at supper and turns your hand over. "You're shaking," {they} say{s}. "What is it?"|{friend} sits down beside you without a word and looks at your hands until you put them in your lap. "What is it?"}|{~"You've been too bright for weeks," {friend} says at supper. "Nobody's that well. What is it?"|{friend} watches you finish a week's reading in an evening and says, quietly, "That isn't you. What is it?"}}
text [fc80a4] = {has(brightwater_want) or has(owls_ink_want): {~晚饭时{friend}抓住你的手腕，把你的手翻过来。“你在发抖，”{they}说。“怎么回事？”|{friend}一言不发地在你身边坐下，一直看着你的手，直到你把手放到膝上。“怎么回事？”}|{~“你已经好几个星期精神好得过头了，”{friend}在晚饭时说。“没人能好成这样。怎么回事？”|{friend}看着你一个晚上读完一个星期的书，轻声说：“这不像你。怎么回事？”}}
# en: Two students on a stone bench in an empty corridor, one holding the other's hand and looking hard at their face.
scene [76be65] = 空荡荡的走廊里，两个学生坐在石凳上，一个握着另一个的手，仔细端详着对方的脸。
# en: Tell {them} the truth
opt.left.label [9b4c6a] = 告诉{them}实话
# en: {~You tell {friend} about the bottle. {they} listen{s} without interrupting, and at the end only say{s}, "All right. Now I know. Sister Amaranth sees this every year, you know."|You tell {them} all of it. {friend} doesn't lecture, and doesn't leave, and mentions the infirmary only once.}
opt.left.say.1 [e77de1] = {~你把瓶子的事告诉了{friend}。{they}听着，没有打断，最后只说：“好。现在我知道了。阿玛兰斯修女每年都见这种事，你知道的。”|你把一切都告诉了{them}。{friend}没有说教，也没有离开，只提了一次医务室。}
# en: Laugh it off
opt.right.label [29c02a] = 一笑带过
# en: {~"Exams," you say, and laugh. {friend} lets the subject go, slowly, and doesn't believe you.|"I'm fine." {friend} looks at you for a long moment. "All right," {they} say{s}. It isn't.}
opt.right.say.1 [2abe7e] = {~“考试嘛，”你说着笑了。{friend}慢慢放下了这个话题，并不相信。|“我没事。”{friend}看了你很久。“好吧，”{they}说。并不好。}

@event wd_bright_grey
# en: The First Thought
title [6e97af] = 醒来的第一个念头
# en: Your first thought on waking is the gold bottle, and so is your second. The Brightwater wore off weeks ago. Everything since has needed a little more pushing than it should.
text [822d6f] = 你醒来的第一个念头是那只金瓶，第二个也是。亮泉水的劲儿几个星期前就过去了。从那以后，每件事都要多推一把才动得了。
# en: A student lying awake in bed at dawn, eyes on the school trunk at the foot of the bed, one hand already reaching for the lid.
scene [b94190] = 黎明时分，一个学生醒着躺在床上，眼睛盯着床尾的学生箱，一只手已经伸向箱盖。
# en: Get up anyway
opt.rise.label [318971] = 照样起床
# en: You get up, dress, and go to every lecture, thinking about the trunk the whole way. It counts. It doesn't feel like it counts.
opt.rise.say.1 [8c89c2] = 你起床，穿衣，去上每一节课，一路上都想着那只箱子。这算数。只是感觉不像算数。
# en: Stay in bed
opt.bed.label [50ea64] = 赖在床上
# en: You sleep through the morning and most of the afternoon. You miss two lectures and feel no better for it, only rested.
opt.bed.say.1 [b4ff70] = 你睡过了整个上午和大半个下午。你错过了两节课，并没觉得好些，只是休息够了。
# en: Drink the bottle in your trunk
opt.dose.label [fd39ce] = 喝下箱子里那瓶
# en: One swallow, and the pushing stops. Everything is easy again at once. You hate how easy that was.
opt.dose.say.1 [8d638b] = 一口下去，那股要推的劲儿没了。一切一下子又变得容易。你恨这有多容易。

@event wd_bright_shakes
# en: Hands That Won't Hold Still
title [90661c] = 停不下来的手
# en: In the practical your hands won't hold still. The vial shivers; the measure goes over the line, twice. The student at the next bench pretends not to see.
text [ce51f6] = 实验课上，你的手停不下来。小瓶在抖；量了两次都超了刻度。隔壁桌的同学假装没看见。
# en: A student at a laboratory bench, their hand trembling so that the liquid in a glass vial shivers.
scene [e1a1ab] = 实验台前，一个学生的手抖得厉害，玻璃小瓶里的液体跟着颤动。
# en: Push through it
opt.push.label [be8889] = 硬撑下去
# en: You grip your wrist with your other hand and finish the measure, badly. Afterwards you sit in the corridor until the shaking stops.
opt.push.say.1 [050528] = 你用另一只手攥住手腕，把这次量完了，量得很糟。课后你坐在走廊里，直到不再发抖。
# en: Ask to sit it out
opt.sit.label [14ec20] = 请求先不做
# en: You ask to sit out. The lecturer looks at your hands, then at your face, and says yes too quickly.
opt.sit.say.1 [9d00c7] = 你请求先不做。讲师看看你的手，又看看你的脸，答应得太快了。
# en: Drink the bottle in your trunk
opt.dose.label [fd39ce] = 喝下箱子里那瓶
# en: You leave the practical "for some air" and drink it in the washroom. Your hands go still. Your face in the mirror doesn't look like a winner's.
opt.dose.say.1 [523922] = 你借口“出去透透气”离开实验课，在盥洗室里喝了它。你的手稳了。镜子里那张脸不像赢家。

@event wd_bright_grisk
# en: Grisk Knows
title [68002d] = 格里斯克知道
# en: Grisk is sitting on your bed. You didn't leave the window open. He holds a gold bottle up to the candle and turns it. "You look peaky," he says kindly. "I have just the thing." {flag(grisk_supply): "The price has gone up, of course. Everything has."|"Not a friend's price, I'm afraid. You never did come to see me."}
text [18470c] = 格里斯克坐在你的床上。你没有开窗。他把一只金瓶举到烛光下转着看。“你脸色不太好，”他和蔼地说。“我正好有对症的东西。”{flag(grisk_supply): “当然，价钱涨了。什么都涨了。”|“恐怕不是朋友价了。你一直没来找过我。”}
# en: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat sitting uninvited on a student's bed at night, a gold bottle held up to the candle.
scene [5b9e67] = 夜里，一个穿天鹅绒马甲的地精不请自来地坐在学生床上，把一只金瓶举到烛光前。
# en: Pay what he asks
opt.buy.label [047cea] = 付他要的价
# en: You pay. He counts it twice, sets the bottle on your pillow like a mint, and leaves by the window.
opt.buy.say.1 [f5c19e] = 你付了钱。他数了两遍，把瓶子像薄荷糖一样放在你的枕头上，从窗口走了。
# en: Show him the window
opt.no.label [d76863] = 请他从窗口出去
# en: "Another night," says Grisk, quite unbothered, and goes out the way he came. You don't sleep, but you didn't buy it.
opt.no.say.1 [05ad93] = “那就改天，”格里斯克毫不在意，从原路出去了。你没睡着，但你没买。

@event wd_ink_blank
# en: A Blank Page
title [161c6d] = 一张白纸
# en: In the lecture, the words go past you like carriages. Two months ago you could have recited them back. Now your page is blank, and the lecturer is already on the next board.
text [70b45c] = 课上，那些话像马车一样从你身边驶过。两个月前你还能一字不差地复述。现在你的纸上一片空白，讲师已经写到下一块黑板了。
# en: A student in a lecture hall staring at a completely blank page, quill hovering, the lecturer's words filling the board.
scene [40709c] = 阶梯教室里，一个学生盯着一张完全空白的纸，羽毛笔悬着，讲师的字写满了黑板。
# en: Sit it out, blank
opt.stare.label [c92946] = 空着坐完
# en: You sit through the hour writing nothing. At the end you have the date at the top of the page, and that's all.
opt.stare.say.1 [609ccf] = 你坐了一个钟头，什么也没写。下课时，你的纸上只有顶上的日期。
# en: Admit you can't follow
opt.ask.label [a6fe19] = 承认自己跟不上
# en: You put your hand up and say you've lost the thread. The lecturer is kind about it, which is worse, and goes back over it slowly, for you.
opt.ask.say.1 [da5265] = 你举手说自己跟丢了。讲师很和善，这更糟，还专门为你慢慢讲了一遍。
# en: Drink the bottle in your trunk
opt.dose.label [fd39ce] = 喝下箱子里那瓶
# en: You drink it behind the lecture hall and go back in. The board snaps into focus mid-sentence. You copy it all, and your hand doesn't feel like yours.
opt.dose.say.1 [a594ea] = 你在讲堂后面喝了它，然后回去。黑板在半句话中间猛地对上了焦。你全抄了下来，那只手不像是你的。

@event wd_ink_empty_well
# en: The Well Runs Dry
title [ace09b] = 井干了
# en: You reach for your magic in the practice room, and there's nothing there: not empty, exactly, but dry, like a well at the end of a long summer. It used to be so easy, on the ink.
text [ed1cb0] = 你在练习室里伸手去够你的魔力，那里什么也没有：不完全是空的，而是干的，像漫长夏天尽头的一口井。用着墨的时候，这曾经那么容易。
# en: A student in a practice room, hand outstretched, a spell fizzling out into a few weak sparks.
scene [91bbcf] = 练习室里，一个学生伸出手，一个法术熄成几点微弱的火星。
# en: Force it
opt.force.label [9d7811] = 硬逼出来
# en: You wring the spell out of yourself. It comes, thin and late. You sit down on the floor afterwards without meaning to.
opt.force.say.1 [2c5654] = 你把法术从自己身上拧了出来。它来了，又细又迟。之后你不由自主地坐到了地上。
# en: Leave it for today
opt.wait.label [1afaa7] = 今天先算了
# en: You put your hands in your pockets and leave the practice for another day. The day after, it's still dry.
opt.wait.say.1 [c8c1d4] = 你把手插进口袋，把练习留到改天。第二天，井还是干的。
# en: Drink the bottle in your trunk
opt.dose.label [fd39ce] = 喝下箱子里那瓶
# en: One dose and the well is full again, brimming, easy. You stand there with sparks on your fingers, ashamed of how good it feels.
opt.dose.say.1 [667d2e] = 一剂下去，井又满了，满得溢出来，轻而易举。你站在那儿，指尖冒着火星，为这感觉有多好而羞愧。

@event wd_ink_dreams
# en: Ink in Your Sleep
title [ba807a] = 梦里的墨
# en: You dream of black ink rising in a well, over your feet, your knees, your mouth, and you wake with the taste of a burnt quill. The candle has burned down, and the castle is very quiet.
text [9a4fd9] = 你梦见黑墨在一口井里上涨，漫过你的脚，你的膝盖，你的嘴，醒来时嘴里有烧焦羽毛笔的味道。蜡烛已经燃尽，城堡里非常安静。
# en: A student sitting up in bed in the dark, sheets tangled, staring at their hands as if expecting ink on them.
scene [738e0f] = 黑暗中，一个学生在床上坐起，床单缠成一团，盯着自己的双手，好像以为上面有墨。
# en: Lie awake till dawn
opt.lie.label [e73fd5] = 醒着躺到天亮
# en: You lie and watch the window go from black to grey. By breakfast you feel scraped thin.
opt.lie.say.1 [5c54bc] = 你躺着看窗户从黑变灰。到早饭时，你觉得自己被刮薄了一层。
# en: Walk the corridors till it passes
opt.walk.label [e3a765] = 在走廊里走到它过去
# en: You walk the dark corridors in your socks until your head clears. A lantern turns a far corner; you don't wait to see whose.
opt.walk.say.1 [747508] = 你穿着袜子在黑暗的走廊里走，直到脑子清醒。远处拐角有一盏提灯转了过来；你没等着看是谁的。
# en: Drink the bottle in your trunk
opt.dose.label [fd39ce] = 喝下箱子里那瓶
# en: You drink it in the dark. The dream doesn't come back. In the morning you can't decide whether that was rescue or surrender.
opt.dose.say.1 [b5b241] = 你在黑暗中喝了它。那个梦没再回来。早上，你分不清那是得救还是投降。

@event amaranth_quit
# en: Sister Amaranth's Remedy
title [85b5c5] = 阿玛兰斯修女的药方
# en: Sister Amaranth looks at you once, the way she looks at a fever chart. "Sit," she says, still rolling a bandage. "I've seen that face before. Brightwater, or the ink? Don't answer. Drink this every morning for a week. It's foul. It works."
text [f1e33e] = 阿玛兰斯修女看了你一眼，就像看一张体温表。“坐，”她说，手里还在卷绷带。“这张脸我见过。亮泉水，还是墨？别回答。这个每天早上喝，喝一个星期。难喝。管用。”
# en: A stern healer in an infirmary looking at a student over a rolled bandage, a bitter-looking cup of medicine on the table between them.
scene [18653b] = 医务室里，一位严厉的医护修女越过一卷绷带看着一个学生，两人之间的桌上放着一杯看起来很苦的药。
# en: Take the remedy
opt.left.label [8d5c87] = 接受这药方
# en: A week of bitter mornings, and her hand held out each time for any bottle you still have. On the eighth day the world comes back in colour. "Drink it all," she says, "and don't come back for the same thing."
opt.left.say.1 [ee8ddd] = 一个星期苦涩的早晨，每次她都伸出手，要走你手上还剩的瓶子。第八天，世界的颜色回来了。“全喝完，”她说，“别再为同一件事回来。”
# en: "It's just a cold, Sister."
opt.right.label [a2ea9f] = “只是感冒，修女。”
# en: "Hm," says Sister Amaranth, and goes back to her bandage. "The door's open. It always is."
opt.right.say.1 [895eb3] = “嗯，”阿玛兰斯修女说，又回去卷她的绷带。“门开着。一直开着。”
